  mn('D-B-M-L-H-W-R', 'Handout: “<b>D</b>on’t <b>B</b>reak <b>M</b>y <b>L</b>ovely <b>H</b>ot <b>W</b>ater <b>R</b>ack” (Development plans, Beneficiaries, MFP, Land alienation, Haats and money, Water, Resolving disputes).'),
  mn('PESA states (10)', '<b>A</b>ndhra Pradesh, <b>C</b>hhattisgarh, <b>G</b>ujarat, <b>H</b>imachal Pradesh, <b>J</b>harkhand, <b>M</b>adhya Pradesh, <b>M</b>aharashtra, <b>O</b>disha, <b>R</b>ajasthan, <b>T</b>elangana: “<b>A</b> <b>C</b>ool <b>G</b>uy <b>H</b>elps <b>J</b>ust <b>M</b>y <b>M</b>other <b>O</b>ften <b>R</b>un <b>T</b>ea.”'),
  bx('ye', '<b>PYQ trap (2013):</b> PESA objectives = self-governance, recognising traditional rights, freeing tribals from exploitation; it does <b>not</b> create autonomous regions (that is Sixth). <b>Undated Prelims:</b> FRA 2006: <b>Gram Sabha</b> initiates determination; <b>Ministry of Tribal Affairs</b> nodal; bamboo = minor forest produce; ST declared by <b>President</b>, not Governor ((b) 2 only). PYQ 2023: 2 of 3 statements correct. Mains: 2013 Art 244 non-implementation (LWE), 2016 why “Scheduled Tribes”, 2017 two legal initiatives vs ST discrimination.'),
  bx('ca', '<span class="tag">In the news · Sep 2026 (verify dates)</span><b>Forest clearance and FRA:</b> Ministry of Tribal Affairs clarified FRA 2006 does not itself require 100% Gram Sabha consent for Stage-II forest clearance. <b>Nautor Land (Ladakh):</b> Ladakh AHDC (Nautor Regularisation) Rules, 2026, over 60,000 acres.'),
